<title>SOUTH KOREA: HYUNDAI ELEC H1 NET FALLS SHARPLY.</title>
<headline>HYUNDAI ELEC H1 NET FALLS SHARPLY.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 1997</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net					14.8 vs    73.1</p>
<p>    Shr (won)				 264 vs   1,588</p>
<p>    Turnover			    1,418.7 vs 1,606.5</p>
<p>    Profit before tax		    17.1 vs    81.6</p>
<p>    Ordinary profit			19.3 vs    81.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Hyundai Electronics Industries Co, a unit of the Hyundai Group, is one of South Korea's top three memory chip makers. A company official attributed the sharp drop in net profit to plunging prices for 16-megabit dynamic random access memories (DRAMs). The company's share capital rose by 10 million shares to 56 million during the 12-month period to June due to its initial public offering in December.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
